      "refersTo": "safety-card",
      "description": "Sage grouping for safe hunt constraints and a reporting action.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-safety\" aria-label=\"Hunt safely\"><strong>A little adventure. A safe one.</strong><div class=\"ds-rules\"><span>1–5 USDC per drop</span><span>Daytime only</span><span>Public places only</span></div><p>Stay on public paths. Exact locations unlock only within 30 m.</p><button class=\"ds-report\">Report this location</button></section>",
      "css": ".ds-safety{background:var(--sage, #eaf4ed);padding:18px;border-radius:16px;margin:26px 0;color:var(--green, #275e43);font-family:\"DM Sans\", sans-serif}.ds-safety strong{font-size:13px}.ds-rules{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 14px;margin-top:14px}.ds-rules span{font-size:11px;font-weight:500}.ds-safety p{font-size:12px;color:inherit;margin:14px 0 0;line-height:1.6}.ds-report{display:inline-flex;min-height:44px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:7px;padding:6px 0;font-family:\"DM Sans\", sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:12px;color:inherit;background:none;border:0;margin-top:4px;cursor:pointer}.ds-report:hover{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}.ds-report:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue, #1760dd);outline-offset:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Hold Claim Control",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "button-primary",
      "description": "Visual specimen of functional hold feedback; this sidecar preview has no claim runtime.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-hold-wrap\"><button class=\"ds-hold\"><span class=\"ds-progress\"></span><span class=\"ds-hold-label\">Hold to claim</span></button><p class=\"ds-help\">Hold for 1.2 seconds. Keyboard: hold Space or Enter.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-hold{min-height:52px;padding:14px 20px;border-radius:12px;border:0;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:10px;font-family:\"DM Sans\", sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;text-align:center;cursor:pointer;transition:background .16s,transform .16s;position:relative;overflow:hidden;width:100%;user-select:none;touch-action:none;min-height:58px;background:var(--blue, #1760dd);color:var(--white, #fff)}.ds-progress{position:absolute;inset:0 auto 0 0;width:0;background:#ffffff35;pointer-events:none}.ds-hold-label{position:relative;z-index:1;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:12px}.ds-hold:hover:not(:disabled){background:#0d4fc5}.ds-hold:active:not(:disabled){transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-hold:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue, #1760dd);outline-offset:4px}.ds-hold:disabled{opacity:.48;cursor:not-allowed}.ds-help{font-family:\"DM Sans\", sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;margin:10px 0;color:var(--muted, #526779);text-align:center}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-hold{transition:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A clear city-walk companion",
    "overview": "Ego uses a clean, light, calm, premium visual world with generous spacing and an original blue coin motif. Chalk-white surfaces, deep ink typography and cobalt money cues make a small mobile utility feel composed and approachable. Quiet sage surfaces frame safety and confirmed outcomes.\n\nWallet-first is a confirmed product decision. The coin is a reusable original geometric signature across the wallet, drop discovery and collectible artwork. Illustrative balances, creators and collectibles remain visibly identified as demo content; visual polish must not imply live funds.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Light tonal surfaces with restrained depth.",
      "Manrope headings and money paired with DM Sans body and controls.",
      "Generous mobile spacing and persistent thumb-reachable navigation.",
      "Original blue coin geometry, circular uncertainty and quiet sage safety cues."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Money Cue Rule",
        "body": "Keep cobalt attached to actions, value and the original coin; preserve sage for safety and confirmation.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Field Rule",
        "body": "Preserve 16px field text and tabular numerals for monetary and distance readings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Pocket Width Rule",
        "body": "Keep form and wallet content constrained; use the desktop rail to add context without stretching mobile controls.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Depth Rule",
        "body": "Use tonal grouping for ordinary surfaces; reserve inset depth for the coin and ambient shadow for map overlays.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do retain the clean light surfaces, generous mobile spacing and original blue coin geometry.",
      "Do pair self-hosted Manrope headings and money with DM Sans body and controls.",
      "Do preserve visible focus, labelled fields, live feedback and safe-area clearance.",
      "Do keep demo identification visible and celebration contingent on confirmed claim state.",
      "Do keep safety and recovery information adjacent to location-based actions.",
      "Do preserve reduced-motion CSS and cancelable hold behavior."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't copy another app's coin artwork or visual identity.",
      "Don't stretch phone forms to fill desktop space.",
      "Don't introduce heavy floating shadows on ordinary cards.",
      "Don't represent illustrative balances or collectibles as live funds.",
      "Don't animate the decorative coin when reduced motion is requested."
    ]
  }
}
